ess cockpit providing excellent visibility for its three-man crew. Powered by two Argus As 410 engines, the Fw 189 had a maximum speed of approximately 355 km/h and a range of about 670 km. It was armed with multiple 7.92mm machine guns and could carry up to four 50 kg bombs. The Fw 189 first entered service in 1940 and was primarily used by the Luftwaffe for short-range reconnaissance missions, especially on the Eastern Front. Its agility and excellent field of view made it effective in its role, earning it the nickname \"Fliegendes Auge\" (Flying Eye) among German forces. Soviet troops referred to it as \"Rama\" (Frame) due to its unique shape. A total of 864 Fw 189 aircraft were produced until mid-1944, with manufacturing taking place in Germany, occupied France, and Czechoslovakia. While primarily a reconnaissance aircraft, variants of the Fw 189 were adapted for roles such as ground attack and night fighting. Despite its relatively slow speed, the Fw 189's maneuverability and design allowed it to perform effectively in its intended roles throughout its service."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnCounterMeasureTriggered","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"spawnCardName":"card_event_production","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/NavalWarfare/t_fw_189.t_fw_189","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FW_189.FW_189","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":296.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fw189_photo","SourceString":"Focke Wulf Fw 189 reconnaissance aircraft. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"Focke Wulf Fw 189 reconnaissance aircraft. Date unknown."